upstream: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/greensock/gsap-skills/main/skills/gsap-utils
verified: 2026-10-30
scope: description-and-links
reason: frontmatter description only; body byte-identical to upstream.
description: 2026-10-30 skill-efficiency pass — frontmatter description rewritten to ≤250 chars (what + boundary front-loaded; Codex truncates at ~250). Body untouched by this pass. Re-apply after a byte-for-byte refresh; see docs/skill-efficiency-audit-2026-10-30.md.
would_lose_if_wired: a byte-for-byte refresh would restore the long upstream description.
refresh_guard: _refresh-vendored.sh skips this directory when .local-fork is present; re-sync body manually, then re-apply the description.
recheck: 2026-11-22 — scope is now `description + 3 links`, no longer description-only. Upstream's links to `random(`, `distribute/` and `splitColor/`
  return HTTP 404 on gsap.com (the first is also a truncated URL, `.../random(`, which is why it was not caught as a missing path). The live pages end in
  the call parentheses; local uses the percent-encoded form `.../random%28%29/`, `.../distribute%28%29/`, `.../splitColor%28%29/` (HTTP 200 each),
  which also stays valid inside a Markdown link where a bare `)` would end it. Re-apply all three after a re-sync. Not reported upstream.
